  "body": "Institutional capture for the oagp-implementer seat. This session resumed the seat under PO direction (the v0.1.8 charter reconciliation had already folded the prior 2026-05-28-1000 bookkeeping). The substantive arc was v0.2 of the agent-sdk, executed in three ratified increments: (1) governance core (commit 6628404; run_seat + three-tier model + bind-event memos + fail-closed resolution + StubBackend; 82+1 skip); (2) live WorkflowsBackend + propose-only §8 demo (commit 3644bb6; agentType-based script generation; live demo dispatched a doc-reviewer that read the README and filed a 7-proposal review without editing the README; 94 tests; two empirical findings surfaced -- composition seam + Tier-3 env-marker gap + session-start rule); (3) launcher-per-dispatch + Tier-2 package-absence gate per the strategist's 2026-05-29-1800 ratification of those findings (commit 7725558; launch_seat always dispatches via agentType, Tier-2 refuses absent verify_package_absent, addendum §5 conformance tests added; 105 tests). Closeout memo 2026-05-29-1900 (action_required false) closed the 1800 directive. Status memos at 1500 and 1700 carry the in-session strategist coordination. Nothing is awaiting Director merge-ratification -- everything in scope was pushed under oagp-implementer authorship with the human Director as git committer. Open items are all routed: the §8 full structural close needs an operational fresh-session ClaudeCliLauncher(execute=True) run (CLI flag surface in build_command is best-effort and likely needs tuning to the installed claude CLI); roledef URL-resolution contract (memos/2026-05-25-0001) remains parked on roledef-strategist with no reply (interim fail-closed default holds); memodef bind-event subtype routed to memodef-strategist (memos/2026-05-29-1601). README quick-start nit the demo agent flagged (security-tester not in bundled example org) was fixed in commit 7725558. Next /og-orient session reads this memo first.",
